   "line": [
    "Kxd8"
   ],
   "spoken": "Trading queens looks like it should ease Black's game, but it does the opposite: the king is dragged to d8, loses the right to castle, and stays stuck in the centre while White pours out pieces.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "A queen trade favours the side whose king it does not strand — here Black loses castling and stays exposed."
